---
description: Superseded tools and modules are relocated to deprecated/, never left in place
alwaysApply: true
---

- When a change supersedes a script, module, tool, or data/spec file (its job is now done by
  something else, or it reads/writes a format that no longer exists), move it to the root
  `deprecated/` folder in that same change. Flat layout; use `git mv` for tracked files.
- Never leave superseded files in place with "unused", "legacy", or "do not run" notes, and never
  ask the user to remember which files are orphaned. Finishing a replacement includes clearing
  out what it replaced.
- Before moving, search the live tree for references (imports, usage strings, docs) and remove or
  update them; nothing outside `deprecated/` may depend on a deprecated file.
- Name every relocated file in chat when reporting the change.
- `deprecated/` and `pxlreact1_archive/` are dead code: do not read, search, run, import, modify,
  or take conventions from them unless the user explicitly asks. Exclude them from searches.
- Throwaway probe/diagnostic scripts made during a task are deleted (not deprecated) before the
  task is reported complete.
